    "rules": [
      {
        "topic": "index",
        "text": "Topics: ca_prelim, ca_lien, ca_waivers, tx_monthly, tx_retainage, tx_waivers, textura, deadlines."
      },
      {
        "topic": "ca_prelim",
        "text": "California preliminary notice (Civil Code 8204): serve within 20 days of first furnishing labor or materials. A late notice still protects work furnished from 20 days before the date of service onward; earlier work is not protected. Not required when the contract is directly with the owner."
      },
      {
        "topic": "ca_lien",
        "text": "California mechanics lien, subcontractor (8414): record within 90 days after completion of the work of improvement, or within 30 days after a Notice of Completion is recorded. Serve the owner (8416). Suit within 90 days of recording (8460). A valid preliminary notice is required."
      },
      {
        "topic": "ca_waivers",
        "text": "Four statutory forms: 8132 conditional progress, 8134 unconditional progress, 8136 conditional final, 8138 unconditional final. An unconditional waiver binds on signature even if payment never arrives: sign one only for money already received. A progress waiver releases everything through its date except what is listed under Exceptions: list retention held and disputed or unpaid extras there. Never sign an unconditional final waiver while retention or any balance is unpaid; offer the 8136 conditional final instead."
      },
      {
        "topic": "tx_monthly",
        "text": "Texas, commercial contracts entered on or after 2022-01-01 (HB 2237): for each month of unpaid work, send notice to the owner and the GC by the 15th day of the third month after the month the work was done (July work: by October 15). Notice may be sent as soon as a payment is late."
      },
      {
        "topic": "tx_retainage",
        "text": "Texas retainage notice (Property Code 53.057): send by the 30th day after the subcontract is completed, terminated or abandoned."
      },
      {
        "topic": "tx_waivers",
        "text": "Texas waivers must substantially follow the statutory forms in Property Code 53.284. Return a GC's custom form, especially one adding indemnity or hold-harmless terms, and offer the statutory form."
      },
      {
        "topic": "textura",
        "text": "Textura: a waiver attached to a draw is released automatically 72 hours after the payment instruction unless the subcontractor files written notice of non-payment within 60 hours of the instruction. File the notice whenever the money is not in the bank."
      },
      {
        "topic": "deadlines",
        "text": "Office policy: a Texas deadline falling on a weekend or holiday moves to the next business day. A California deadline falling on a weekend is met on the business day before it. Count days from the day after the triggering event."
      }
    ],
